# Build output. The bundle is generated by ./build-app.sh, including the icon and
# the patched copy of vpnc-script, so nothing in it is a source of truth.
AnywayConnect.app/
AnywayConnect.app.staging/
*.iconset/
*.icns
build/

# Distribution archives, left behind by scripts/notarize.sh and by release packaging.
*.zip
*.zip.sha256

# Runtime state. Lives under ~/.config/anyway-connect/ normally; this guards against
# a stray copy inside the checkout, which would mean committing tunnel logs and — if
# a connect were interrupted at the wrong moment — a live session cookie.
state/

# Agent / editor workspace
.kiro/

# Agent task artifacts: investigations, designs, reviews, plans and verification
# evidence, regenerated per task. Useful while the work is in flight and referenced
# from commit messages, but it is scratch output rather than a source of truth, and it
# grows without bound. Anything here worth keeping gets promoted into docs/ deliberately.
.agents/

# Worktrees. `git worktree add .worktrees/<name>` keeps its checkout here; the branch
# is already in the repository, so the directory is a second copy of the tree.
.worktrees/

# Diagnostic output. scripts/anyway-diag.sh now writes its own report.txt into a
# persistent bundle under ~/Library/Logs/anyway-connect/, so redirecting its stdout
# into the checkout is no longer necessary — but it was the only way to keep the
# verdict before that, and the habit outlives the reason. A captured run of a wedged
# network names interfaces, gateways, resolvers and loaded security extensions; it is
# incident evidence, not a source of truth, and it does not belong in history.
anyway-diag*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store
